; The GPU-process sandbox profile for this port.
;
; Like the webpushd profile beside it, this one has no Mavericks-era upstream ancestor to
; recover: the GPU process postdates 10.9 by a decade, so upstream never wrote a version of it
; in this OS's sandbox vocabulary. Feeding upstream's own
; Source/WebKit/GPUProcess/mac/com.apple.WebKit.GPUProcess.sb.in to 10.9's real compiler fails
; at `line 88: unbound variable: nvram*`, and initializeSandbox() CRASH()es rather than launch a
; process whose profile will not apply.
;
; It is therefore written in the vocabulary 10.9's compiler accepts -- `(import "system.sb")`,
; `iokit-open` rather than iokit-open-service/iokit-open-user-client, no with-filter, no
; file-map-executable, no message filters -- and grants what this port's GPU process actually
; does: DOM and canvas rasterization, and WebGL. Media playback, capture and WebRTC codecs all stay
; in the web process, where this port's GStreamer engine lives (UseGPUProcessForMediaEnabled,
; CaptureVideoInGPUProcessEnabled and WebRTCPlatformCodecsInGPUProcessEnabled are all false for
; USE(GSTREAMER)), so upstream's AVFoundation playback, capture and codec grants -- and the camera,
; microphone and TCC rules that go with them -- have no counterpart here.
;
; The font, ColorSync and CoreGraphics rules are the ones the recovered 10.9 WebProcess profile
; carries, because rasterizing is the work that moved: the same CoreText and CoreGraphics paths
; run here now instead of there.
;
; Copyright (C) 2024 Apple Inc. All rights reserved.
;
; Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without
; modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions
; are met:
